SUMMARY:Bearwallow Mountain Trail\nFull Moon Hike - 2.1 mi. 587' g.
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThis Full Moon\, commonly known as
  the Buck Moon\, will have an illumination of 99.8% at a distance of 248\,
 926 miles. Current weather forecast calls for sunny skies and a low that e
 vening around 63. Once the sun sets it may become a little chilly at 4\,23
 2' elevation so consider bringing a light jacket. The ascent is around one
  mile and will take us an estimated 30 minutes but it's challenging enough
  to elevate your heart rate. For safety purposes we will take the wide fir
 e service road back to our cars.\n\nWe will gather at the Fresh Market on 
 Hendersonville Rd. at 6:15 and depart at 6:30\, taking the "back way" as H
 ighway 74 is still limited to local traffic beyond Gerton. Parking can be 
 tight at the trail head so carpooling is essential.\n\nNOTE! Bring a head 
 lamp or flashlight with a red lens "for emergency purposes" only. We do no
 t use flashlights as it will be bright enough to see our way down the wide
  gravel road and they detract from the experience. I'll also try and remem
 ber to bring some glow sticks to attach around our ankles.\nIf you have ni
 ght vision problems or are unstable in low light situations this hike is p
 robably not for you.\n\nWear appropriate shoes\, bring water\, snacks\, an
 d maybe a lite blanket to sit on. Poles are optional.\n\nSunset is at 8:36
  p:m and the Moon rises at 8:55 p:m. Plan on relaxing and enjoying this ce
 lestial event with others. We will begin to head back down around 9:15 - 9
 :30. I estimate getting back to our cars around 10:00 p:m.\nGuests need to
  join Asheville Hiking Group and sign up for this hike on their own.\n\nBe
 ing how erratic our weather has been lately\, if there is a change in the 
 forecast that necessitates canceling\, I will do so by 5:00 p:m Wednesday.
  Only sign up if you truly plan to attend. If you must cancel\, do so asap
  to allow any on wait list ample time. No shows = not cool.\n\nAny questio
 ns please feel free to message me through this Meetup app.\n\nLegal Stuff:
  This Asheville Hiking Group (AHG) event involves hiking and\, possibly\, 
 transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible f
 or their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, phy
 sical conditioning\, equipment\,and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to 
 oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Gro
 up can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume ful
 l responsibility for any injuries or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315824234
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
